        "start_line": 2502,
        "end_line": 2526,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "ESP-specific implicit matches injected into generic flex parser helper",
        "explanation": "mlx5dr_definer_get_flex_parser_fc is a shared helper. Its only callers are the IPv6 routing extension (SRv6) and eCPRI conversion paths; no ESP code calls it. In non-relaxed mode the new block always adds an implicit outer match. It requires IP protocol == IPPROTO_ESP when outer IP_PROTOCOL is unset, or L4 dport == 4500 when the outer L4 is UDP and no dport is set. This changes the semantics of existing rules. eCPRI over Ethernet gets an impossible IP protocol == 50 match. eCPRI over UDP without an explicit dport is forced to dport 4500. Inner (tunnelled) SRv6 matches get outer IP protocol == ESP. All of these rules then fail to match traffic they used to match.",
        "suggestion": "Move the ESP ip_protocol/udp-port implicit match into the ESP item conversion function (or a dedicated helper it calls), and keep get_flex_parser_fc generic.",
        "evidence": "\t/* To match on ESP we must match on ip_protocol and optionally on l4_dport */",
        "confidence": 0.8,
        "id": "89f048ffe13f",
        "hunk_id": "drivers/net/mlx5/hws/mlx5dr_definer.c#4",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "drivers/net/mlx5/hws/mlx5dr_definer.c",
        "start_line": 2701,
        "end_line": 2701,
