        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "eCPRI rules now get spurious ESP protocol/port match",
        "explanation": "Through this call, the eCPRI conversion now runs the ESP implicit-match logic in get_flex_parser_fc. When not relaxed, eCPRI over Ethernet gets an outer IP protocol == 50 match, so the rule can never hit. eCPRI over UDP without a dport gets dport == 4500 and misses eCPRI traffic.",
        "suggestion": "Remove the ESP logic from get_flex_parser_fc so eCPRI does not inherit it.",
